ge)/features/high-availability.mdx","High Availability","Active/active and active/standby Phoenix client wiring across two HBase clusters, with graceful failover that lets writes drain server-side before the peer is promoted.","/docs/features/high-availability",{"_41":288},"(multi-page)/features/query-server.mdx","Query Server","Deploy and use Phoenix Query Server (PQS), including client access, impersonation, metrics, and load-balancing configuration.","/docs/features/query-server",{"_41":293},"(multi-page)/features/phoenix-sync-table.mdx","PhoenixSyncTable Tool","Detect data divergence between a source and a target Phoenix table across two HBase clusters via a chunked hash comparison driven by MapReduce.","/docs/features/phoenix-sync-table",{"_41":298},"(multi-page)/features/bulk-loading.mdx","Bulk Loading","Load Phoenix tables with PSQL and MapReduce-based CSV/JSON bulk loaders, including options, permissions, and tuning notes.","/docs/features/bulk-loading",{"_41":303},"(multi-page)/features/change-data-capture.mdx","Change Data Capture (CDC)","Query row-level change events on a Phoenix table using standard SQL — pull pre/post images and change deltas with bounded, resumable reads.","/docs/features/change-data-capture",{"_41":308},"(multi-page)/features/bson.mdx","Document Data: BSON","Store, query, filter, and atomically update Binary JSON (BSON) documents inside a Phoenix table — without round-tripping the document to the client.","/docs/features/bson",{"_41":313},"(multi-page)/features/varbinary-encoded.mdx","VARBINARY_ENCODED","A variable-length binary type that sorts correctly anywhere in a composite key — use it for row keys, index keys, and row value constructors that contain binary data.","/docs/features/varbinary-encoded",{"_41":318},"(multi-page)/features/dynamic-columns.mdx","Dynamic Columns","Define and query late-bound dynamic columns in Phoenix when full schema cannot be declared upfront.","/docs/features/dynamic-columns",{"_41":323},"(multi-page)/features/multi-tenancy.mdx","Multi-tenancy","Use multi-tenant tables, tenant-specific connections, and tenant views to isolate tenant data in Phoenix.","/docs/features/multi-tenancy",{"_41":328},"(multi-page)/features/conditional-ttl.mdx","Conditional TTL","Express row expiration as a SQL boolean expression evaluated against the row itself.","/docs/features/conditional-ttl",{"_41":333},"(multi-page)/features/view-ttl.mdx","View TTL","Per-view retention on top of a shared base table — different views can age data out on different schedules without splitting the table.","/docs/features/view-ttl",{"_41":338},"(multi-page)/features/ttl.mdx","TTL","Phoenix TTL flavors (time-based, view, conditional) and the IS_STRICT_TTL property that controls visibility of expired rows.","/docs/features/ttl",{"_41":343},"(multi-page)/features/views.mdx","Views","Define updatable and read-only Phoenix views over shared HBase tables, including indexing behavior and limitations.","/docs/features/views",{"_41":348},"(multi-page)/features/table-sampling.mdx","Table Sampling","Use TABLESAMPLE in Phoenix for Bernoulli-style sampling, with performance notes, repeatability behavior, and tuning guidance.","/docs/features/table-sampling",{"_41":353},"Segment Scan","Get N evenly-bucketed key ranges for a Phoenix table so a client can drive a parallel full-table scan.",{"_41":6},"(multi-page)/features/skip-scan.mdx","Skip Scan","How Phoenix Skip Scan uses key-range hints to efficiently skip non-matching row-key regions.","/docs/features/skip-scan",{"_41":361},"(multi-page)/features/salted-tables.mdx","Salted Tables","Use SALT_BUCKETS to reduce HBase hotspotting and understand scan, split, and ordering behavior for salted tables.","/docs/features/salted-tables",{"_41":366},"(multi-page)/features/paged-queries.mdx","Paged Queries","Use row value constructors and OFFSET/LIMIT for efficient paged query patterns in Phoenix.","/docs/features/paged-queries",{"_41":371},"(multi-page)/features/phoenix-row-timestamp.mdx","PHOENIX_ROW_TIMESTAMP()","Read the per-row last-modified timestamp Phoenix maintains automatically — usable in projections, predicates, and indexes for fast time-bounded reads.","/docs/features/phoenix-row-timestamp",{"_41":376},"(multi-page)/features/row-timestamp-column.mdx","Row Timestamp Column","Map HBase row timestamps to a Phoenix primary-key column and use ROW_TIMESTAMP in table design and upserts.","/docs/features/row-timestamp-column",{"_41":381},"(multi-page)/features/statistics-collection.mdx","Statistics Collection","How Phoenix collects and uses guidepost statistics for query parallelization, with commands and configuration.","/docs/features/statistics-collection",{"_41":386},"(multi-page)/features/namespace-mapping.mdx","Namespace Mapping","Enable Phoenix schema-to-namespace mapping in HBase, including configuration, migration, and behavior by table type.","/docs/features/namespace-mapping",{"_41":391},"(multi-page)/features/atomic-upsert.mdx","Atomic Upsert","Use UPSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY for atomic row-level updates in Phoenix, with examples and limitations.","/docs/features/atomic-upsert",{"_41":396},"(multi-page)/features/storage-formats.mdx","Storage Formats","Configure Phoenix column mapping and immutable storage encoding for better storage efficiency and performance.","/docs/features/storage-formats",{"_41":401},"(multi-page)/features/eventually-consistent-indexes.mdx","Eventually Consistent Global Indexes","Global secondary indexes maintained asynchronously off the data-table write path — for write-heavy workloads that can tolerate a bounded staleness window on the index in exchange for higher write throughput.","/docs/features/eventually-consistent-indexes",{"_41":406},"(multi-page)/features/secondary-indexes.mdx","Secondary Indexes","Concepts, setup, consistency guarantees, and tooling for Phoenix secondary indexes.","/docs/features/secondary-indexes",{"_41":411},"(multi-page)/features/user-defined-functions.mdx","User-defined Functions","Create, deploy, and manage custom Phoenix UDFs with configuration, implementation steps, and known limitations.","/docs/features/user-defined-functions",{"_41":416},"(multi-page)/features/transactions.mdx","Transactions","Configure and use transactional tables in Phoenix with Tephra, including setup steps and limitations.","/docs/features/transactions",{"_41":421},"Fundamentals",[431,432,433,434,435,436,437],"(multi-page)/fundamentals",{"_32":430},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/meta.json",{"_11":468,"_19":36,"_13":469,"_25":470,"_22":-7,"_7":471,"_30":472},{"_11":463,"_19":36,"_13":464,"_25":465,"_22":-7,"_7":466,"_30":467},{"_11":458,"_19":36,"_13":459,"_25":460,"_22":-7,"_7":461,"_30":462},{"_11":453,"_19":36,"_13":454,"_25":455,"_22":-7,"_7":456,"_30":457},{"_11":448,"_19":36,"_13":449,"_25":450,"_22":-7,"_7":451,"_30":452},{"_11":443,"_19":36,"_13":444,"_25":445,"_22":-7,"_7":446,"_30":447},{"_11":438,"_19":36,"_13":439,"_25":440,"_22":-7,"_7":441,"_30":442},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/performance-testing.mdx","Performance Testing","Use Pherf to generate data and run Phoenix performance tests.","/docs/fundamentals/performance-testing",{"_41":438},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/performance.mdx","Performance","Historical Phoenix performance comparisons and feature-level improvements for scans, salting, and query execution.","/docs/fundamentals/performance",{"_41":443},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/backward-compatibility.mdx","Backward Compatibility","Phoenix upgrade compatibility across patch, minor, and major releases.","/docs/fundamentals/backward-compatibility",{"_41":448},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/configuration.mdx","Configuration","Phoenix configuration properties and tuning defaults.","/docs/fundamentals/configuration",{"_41":453},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/tuning-guide.mdx","Tuning Guide","Best practices for tuning Phoenix schema, indexes, queries, and write paths for read/write performance.","/docs/fundamentals/tuning-guide",{"_41":458},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/client-classpath-and-jdbc-url.mdx","Client Classpath and JDBC URL","Configure Phoenix thick-client classpath and JDBC URLs.","/docs/fundamentals/client-classpath-and-jdbc-url",{"_41":463},"(multi-page)/fundamentals/building.mdx","Building","Build Apache Phoenix and add it to Maven-based projects.","/docs/fundamentals/building",{"_41":468},"(multi-page)#5","Development","(multi-page)/faq.mdx","FAQ","Frequently asked question about Phoenix","CircleQuestionMark","/docs/faq",{"_41":475},"(multi-page)/installation.mdx","Installation","Install and configure Apache Phoenix clients and server components.","Wrench","/docs/installation",{"_41":481},"(multi-page)/quick-start.mdx","Quick Start","Phoenix in 15 minutes or less.","Rocket","/docs/quick-start",{"_41":487},"(multi-page)/index.mdx","Overview","OLTP and operational analytics for Apache Hadoop.","BookOpen","/docs",{"_41":493},"(multi-page)#0","Getting Started"]
